            <ArticleTitle>Mesenteric desmoid tumour masquerading as a fat-containing cystic mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e200-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1259/bjr/68468861</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mesenteric desmoid tumour (MDT) is an uncommon neoplasm that typically presents as a solid soft-tissue mass on cross-sectional imaging. MDT manifesting as a fat-containing cystic mass on CT has not been described in the literature. We report such an unusual case with clinicopathological correlation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
